    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n1. **Governance module exports** (src/finetune/index.js): Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` so the test can import them directly. The test was failing because it tried to call `.join()` on an undefined value\u2014the export was only available through the default export, not as a named export.\n\n2. **Toxicity metric signature** (src/eval/metrics.js): Removed the `bannedTerms` parameter from `toxicityMetric()`. The function was being called with both outputs and references by `runEvaluations()`, but references were being misinterpreted as banned terms, causing false positives. The function now always uses the default banned terms list.",
